ery: check for https:// only, validate domain against allowlist, implement certificate pinning for OAuth endpoints\",\n    \"Add response schema validation in token refresh flow using Zod or similar before accessing response.data fields\",\n    \"Reduce MCP elicitation timeout from 120_000ms to 30_000ms (30 seconds) to prevent extended unmonitored operation\",\n    \"Add https:// requirement to ConfigSchema for baseUrl validation: z.string().url().refine(u => u.startsWith('https://'), 'Must use HTTPS')\",\n    \"Validate that apiKeyEnv environment variables are defined at startup in createEngine() before attempting to use them\",\n    \"Improve process alive check to distinguish between EPERM (process exists, can't signal) and ESRCH (process doesn't exist)\",\n    \"Add rate limiting to credential refresh to prevent token refresh bombing attacks\",\n    \"Add CSRF token validation to OAuth callback handling (when implemented)\"\n  ]\n}\n```\n\n**Key Risk Summary:**\n\nThe main vulnerabilities center around **credential storage and OAuth handling**. The encryption key is insufficiently random (high), file permissions are not restricted (high), and MCP OAuth discovery lacks transport security (high). Medium-severity issues include missing validation in refresh flows and overly-long timeouts. The codebase would benefit from adopting industry-standard patterns: system keychains for secrets, HTTPS enforcement, and proper OAuth response validation.\n",
